Run davinci-resolve-mcp as the desktop user running DaVinci Resolve, with
Preferences > General > External scripting using set to Local.
Resolve 21.1's scripting module under /opt/resolve/ResolvePython/lib/modules
is detected automatically. For older releases, enable USE=developer on
media-video/davinci-resolve-studio to install the scripting SDK.
RESOLVE_SCRIPT_API and RESOLVE_SCRIPT_LIB can override the default
/opt/resolve installation paths; PYTHONPATH can provide a custom module path.

MCP client configuration:
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "davinci-resolve": {
      "command": "/usr/bin/davinci-resolve-mcp"
    }
  }
}

The default transport is stdio. Add --full for the granular tools.
davinci-resolve-mcp-control-panel launches the local browser interface;
use --help to see its options.

Logs, preferences and runtime state default to
${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/davinci-resolve-mcp.
DAVINCI_RESOLVE_MCP_STATE_DIR overrides this directory. Upstream's individual
log/preference path overrides continue to work. Automatic upstream update
checks are disabled by the launcher; update the package through Portage.

This package installs the Python server, local control panel and knowledge
documents. The separate Node.js resolve-advanced server and npm bootstrapper
are not installed. Optional analysis programs such as ffmpeg, transcription
engines and vision models are detected at runtime.

MCP 2.2.0 cannot import the FastMCP API used by this release. The ebuild
therefore uses MCP 1.30.0; recent Pydantic 2.13.5 and Starlette 1.7.0 were
tested successfully. Gentoo currently marks the required HTTPX 0.x package
deprecated, so pkgcheck reports that dependency warning.
